1
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:25,344
Already after a couple of weeks, small green balls appeared -

2
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:26,112
where the rhubarb leaves stretched after the sun

3
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:28,160
Then came the drought.

4
00:00:28,928 --> 00:00:32,768
The muddy soil that I touched around solidified to a hard crust

5
00:00:33,024 --> 00:00:39,168
And burst into a grid pattern so my rhubarb jam looked like the pictures from a drying disaster in Africa.

6
00:00:39,424 --> 00:00:40,192
null

7
00:00:40,448 --> 00:00:43,264
The rhubarb cannot be able to get through.

8
00:00:43,776 --> 00:00:45,056
But it made the weeds.

9
00:00:45,824 --> 00:00:51,968
Admittedly, the quick root had to make an effort, but thistles and the horse hood seemed to be happy.

10
00:01:43,936 --> 00:01:45,728
The plan was excellent.

11
00:01:45,984 --> 00:01:52,128
I had spent a lot of time pondering how I want a sensible hen house that would work just as well

12
00:01:52,384 --> 00:01:53,408
For me as for the chickens.

13
00:01:53,664 --> 00:01:56,224
It was the reality that was the problem.

14
00:01:56,736 --> 00:02:01,856
I want dense walls in the hen house because pulls are worse than cold for chickens

15
00:02:02,112 --> 00:02:06,464
But when I started to put up slices on the walls, the screws did not attach.

16
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:08,768
The old wood was rotten.

17
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:14,400
And when I started changing the old board wall, the rules behind were also rotten.

18
00:02:14,912 --> 00:02:16,192
The sill was the route.

19
00:02:16,704 --> 00:02:21,056
So I had to make a decision for how carefully I would be with the renovation.

20
00:02:21,568 --> 00:02:24,896
Chicken house renovation is starting to grow uncontrolled.

21
00:02:25,152 --> 00:02:31,296
To nail over the rotten wood would do all renovation to wasted work that must

22
00:02:31,552 --> 00:02:34,368
Made about the day the barn began to sack together.

23
00:02:34,624 --> 00:02:37,184
So I changed the sill and I changed rules.

24
00:02:37,440 --> 00:02:41,024
And the project I set aside for a week for just rolled on.

25
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:45,888
Every rotting plank I removed revealed more and more work.

26
00:02:46,144 --> 00:02:49,728
Meanwhile, the weeds were flourished in my rhubarb cultivation.

27
00:02:51,008 --> 00:02:53,056
The chickens were hatched and began to grow.

28
00:02:53,312 --> 00:02:58,176
After a week, the chickens are no longer allowed because they dust.

29
00:02:58,432 --> 00:03:01,504
It is a fact that perhaps only chicken owners know.

30
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:07,904
Chicken birds - however nice they are - have the ability to create a dust layer that settles

31
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:09,952
Everywhere in the room they live in.

32
00:04:02,176 --> 00:04:06,016
The chicken move to the guest cottage was just a temporary solution.

33
00:04:06,272 --> 00:04:12,416
So on the list of jobs that was in a hurry, I therefore had to add a new point: to create a temporary

34
00:04:12,672 --> 00:04:13,696
Accommodation for the chickens.

35
00:04:13,952 --> 00:04:20,095
The renovation of the chicken house was stopped and instead I started rebuilding the old pigsty

36
00:04:20,351 --> 00:04:21,887
to temporary chicken accommodation.

37
00:04:22,143 --> 00:04:27,519
Now I ignore the rotting planks but just slammed slices on the walls.

38
00:04:27,775 --> 00:04:33,919
Put nets over the old rat holes, compost grates over all other openings and a plastic mat on the floor.

39
00:04:34,175 --> 00:04:37,247
On with litter and then the chickens had to move in.

40
00:04:38,015 --> 00:04:39,295
And the weeds grew.

41
00:04:40,319 --> 00:04:41,855
It will never be as you imagined.

42
00:04:45,439 --> 00:04:46,463
null
